Limitations of this first version

This approach only reads messages currently rendered in the page. ChatGPT virtualizes long conversations, so older messages may not be present in the DOM until you scroll to them. Also, the timestamp we're assigning is the extraction time, not the original message time.

For a production-quality extractor, I recommend a different architecture:

Phase 1: Get the current conversation ID from the URL.

Phase 2: Intercept the network requests/responses that fetch the conversation data, which often contain the complete message tree and richer metadata (IDs, timestamps, model, etc.).

Phase 3: Normalize the data into your unified JSON schema.

Phase 4: Add adapters for Gemini, Claude, Perplexity, Grok, and others.

That network-based approach is significantly more robust than relying on the page's HTML structure and is the direction I'd recommend as we scale this project.
